<title>GREECE: GREEK VERNICOS SAYS 96 DIV/SHARE UP 23.8 PCT.</title>
<headline>GREEK VERNICOS SAYS 96 DIV/SHARE UP 23.8 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Vernicos Yachts said its 1996 dividend per share will rise 23.8 percent to 120 drachmas from 96.9 drachmas in 1995, company president George Vernicos told Reuters.</p>
<p>But net profits fell 7.2 percent to 230 million drachmas from 248 million in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;I always refer to my firm as being the first recreation yachts company to become listed in a stock exchange, worldwide,&quot; he said. --Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
